{%- comment -%}
  Zaria - Made to Measure form for ready-to-wear garments (Abaya / Jalabiya / Sheila).
  Renders INSIDE the product form ({% form 'product' %}), so every choice is captured as a
  line-item property and shows on the Shopify order + emails.
  Ready to Wear -> the house standard size + the Size Chart. Made to Order -> cut at the fitting, with
  numbered measurement points that light up as each cm dropdown is completed. Usage:
  {% render 'zaria-measure-form', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Optional parameters, for the design brief which renders this form without a product:
    show_comment: false  - the brief has its own description box, so drop this one
    custom_only: true    - every piece a brief describes is cut to order, so there is no
                           Ready to Wear to choose: the measurements open straight away
  With no product at all the form falls to its cut-to-order side, which is what a brief is.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign zmm_show_comment = true -%}
{%- if show_comment == false -%}{%- assign zmm_show_comment = false -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign zmm_customonly = false -%}
{%- if custom_only == true -%}{%- assign zmm_customonly = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- assign zmm_is_abaya = false -%}
{%- if product.type == 'Abaya' or product.tags contains 'Abaya' -%}{%- assign zmm_is_abaya = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Ready to Wear only. The older ready-to-wear jalabiyas and abayas are cut and finished before they
  reach the shop, so there is nothing to measure: they take a standard size and the made-to-measure
  half of this form would promise something the atelier is not offering on them. Carrying the tag
  "No Customisation" leaves the size and the size chart and drops the Made to Order mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The nine from the client's own measurement guide (2026-11-17), in its order and its words:
  neck depth, neck width, sleeve length, armhole, chest, waist, hips, full length, shoulder
  width. Rows are "Label:min:max:what to measure", separated by | rather than , because the
  guide's wording has commas in it.

  min and max are HALF inches, since the dropdown steps in halves: 32 to 64 is 16 to 32 in.
  **Chest, waist and hips are flat widths**, measured across the garment lying down, not
  around the body, which is why they read about half of a body measurement. The note under
  the drawing says so, and doubling is left to the atelier rather than to the customer.

  The numbered points on the drawing are matched to these by forloop.index, so the circles
  have to move with any change to this line.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign zmm_fields = "Neck depth:6:24:Neckline shoulder level to the lowest point of the V|Neck width:8:22:Straight across the neck opening, from one side to the other|Sleeve length:30:56:Shoulder seam to the cuff, along the outer sleeve|Armhole:26:52:Around the complete armhole seam, where the sleeve joins the body|Chest:32:64:Across the garment, just below the armholes|Waist:30:64:Across the garment, at the natural waist level|Hips:34:72:Across the garment, at the fullest hip level|Full length:96:132:Highest shoulder point beside the neck, straight down to the hem|Shoulder width:26:40:Across the upper back, from one shoulder seam to the other" | split: '|' -%}
{%- assign zmm_nocust = false -%}
{%- if product.tags contains 'No Customisation' -%}{%- assign zmm_nocust = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  No comment box on a finished piece (client, 2026-11-16). It is cut, sewn and sitting on the
  rail, so there is nothing a preference or a deadline can change about it, and asking invites a
  request the atelier cannot honour. It stays on the made-to-order side, where the note is read
  before the piece is cut. The Sheila choice on an abaya is a real option either way and keeps
  its place in the same panel.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if zmm_nocust -%}{%- assign zmm_show_comment = false -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  field spec: "Label:half-inch-min:half-inch-max" (value = h / 2, so half-inch steps). Order =
  diagram numbers. The figures are inches, matching the size chart; they used to be written into
  the order as centimetres, which was simply wrong. Each option now carries both units.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  .zmm{margin:2px 0 18px;padding:4px 0}
  .zmm__top{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .zmm__head{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#161616;margin:0 0 4px}
  .zmm__head .req{color:var(--wine,#7a1f34)}
  .zmm__sub:empty{display:none}
  .zmm__sub{font-size:13px;color:var(--zf-hint);margin:0;max-width:52ch;line-height:1.65}
  .zmm__modes{display:flex;gap:10px;margin:14px 0 0}
  .zmm__modes[hidden]{display:none}
  .zmm__units{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a79f93;margin:14px 0 0}
  .zmm__mode{flex:1 1 0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;cursor:pointer;
    height:var(--zf-h);border:1px solid var(--zf-line);background:var(--zf-bg);padding:0 12px;font-size:12px;
    letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4a4a4a;
    transition:border-color .18s ease,color .18s ease,background .18s ease}
  .zmm__mode:hover{border-color:var(--zf-line-hover);color:#161616}
  .zmm__mode input{accent-color:var(--wine,#7a1f34);width:16px;height:16px;margin:0}
  .zmm__mode.is-active{border-color:var(--wine,#7a1f34);color:#161616;background:#fbf7f8}
  .zmm__panel{margin-top:18px}
  .zmm__panel[hidden]{display:none}
  .zmm select,.zmm textarea{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:inherit;font-size:var(--zf-size);
    letter-spacing:.01em;color:var(--zf-ink);background:var(--zf-bg);border:1px solid var(--zf-line);
    border-radius:var(--zf-radius);transition:border-color .18s ease,box-shadow .18s ease}
  .zmm select{height:var(--zf-h);padding:0 var(--zf-pr) 0 var(--zf-px);cursor:pointer;
    -webkit-appearance:none;-moz-appearance:none;appearance:none;
    background-image:var(--zf-arrow);background-repeat:no-repeat;
    background-position:var(--zf-arrow-pos);background-size:var(--zf-arrow-size)}
  .zmm textarea{min-height:96px;padding:14px var(--zf-px);resize:vertical;line-height:1.6}
  .zmm select:hover,.zmm textarea:hover{border-color:var(--zf-line-hover)}
  .zmm select:focus,.zmm textarea:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--zf-line-focus);box-shadow:var(--zf-ring)}
  .zmm select option{color:var(--zf-ink)}
  .zmm select option:disabled{color:var(--zf-disabled)}
  .zmm__label{font-size:var(--zf-label-size);letter-spacing:var(--zf-label-track);text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--zf-label);margin:0 0 var(--zf-label-gap);line-height:1.4}
  .zmm__label .req{color:var(--wine,#7a1f34)}
  .zmm__hint{font-size:var(--zf-hint-size);color:var(--zf-hint);margin:12px 0 0;line-height:1.65}

  /* Ready to Wear */
  .zmm__ready-grid{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:2px}
  .zmm__ready-grid .zmm__label{margin:0;white-space:nowrap}
  .zmm__ready-grid select{width:auto;min-width:188px}
  .zmm__ready-grid .zmm__chart{margin-left:4px;padding-left:18px;border-left:1px solid #ece8e2}
  .zmm__ready-grid .zmm__chart .zsc__open{padding:0}
  @media (max-width:600px){
    .zmm__ready-grid{gap:9px 16px}
    .zmm__ready-grid .zmm__label{flex:0 0 100%}
    .zmm__ready-grid select{min-width:0;width:160px;flex:0 0 auto}
    .zmm__ready-grid .zmm__chart{margin-left:0;padding-left:0;border-left:0;flex:0 1 auto}
  }

  /* Made to Order */
  {%- comment -%}A little wider than the old sketch needed: the guide carries nine numbers and fine rules.{%- endcomment -%}
  .zmm__visual{display:grid;grid-template-columns:clamp(210px,24vw,290px) 1fr;gap:clamp(18px,3vw,34px);align-items:start}
  .zmm__figure{position:sticky;top:14px}
  .zmm__figure svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}
  .zmm__figsay{font-size:11px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--zf-hint,#8a8178);margin:8px 0 0;text-align:center}
  .zmm__guidewrap{position:relative;line-height:0}
  .zmm__guide{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}
  .zmm__dot{position:absolute;width:5.6%;aspect-ratio:1;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);border-radius:50%;
    display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:var(--wine,#7a1f34);color:#fff;
    font-family:inherit;font-size:clamp(8px,1.05vw,11px);line-height:1;opacity:0;pointer-events:none;
    transition:opacity .2s ease,box-shadow .2s ease}
  .zmm__dot.is-done{opacity:1}
  .zmm__dot.is-active{opacity:1;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(122,31,52,.16)}
  .zmm__figcap{text-align:center;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a79f93;margin:10px 0 0}
  .zmm__mark{transition:transform .18s ease}
  .zmm__mark circle{fill:#fff;stroke:#c9a86a;stroke-width:1.4;transition:fill .18s ease,stroke .18s ease}
  .zmm__mark text{fill:#7a6a3f;stroke:none;font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;transition:fill .18s ease;paint-order:stroke fill}
  .zmm__mark.is-done circle{fill:var(--wine,#7a1f34);stroke:var(--wine,#7a1f34)}
  .zmm__mark.is-done text{fill:#fff}
  .zmm__mark.is-active{transform:scale(1.28)}
  .zmm__mark.is-active circle{stroke:#161616}

  .zmm__fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px var(--zf-gap);align-items:stretch}
  .zmm__fname .req{color:var(--wine,#7a1f34)}
  .zmm__fields--ready{margin-top:4px}
  .zmm__readyfoot{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px 20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px}
  .zmm__readyfoot .zmm__hint{margin:0;flex:1 1 280px;max-width:54ch}
  .zmm__readyfoot .zmm__chart{flex:0 0 auto}
  .zmm__readyfoot .zsc__open{padding:0}
  {%- comment -%}
    A row's two boxes line up however long the wording above them runs. The guide's sentences
    wrap to one, two or three lines, and with the boxes following the text straight down, one
    column sat lower than the other and the form read as a mess (client, 2026-11-17). The field
    fills its row and the box is pushed to the foot of it, so the two always meet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  .zmm__field{display:flex;flex-direction:column;position:relative;height:100%}
  .zmm__field > select{margin-top:auto}
  {%- comment -%}What to measure, in the guide's own words, under the name it belongs to.{%- endcomment -%}
  .zmm__fsay{display:block;font-size:11px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--zf-hint,#8a8178);margin:3px 0 8px;max-width:34ch}
  .zmm__field--full{grid-column:1 / -1}
  .zmm__fhead{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:0 0 var(--zf-label-gap);min-height:20px}
  .zmm__num{flex:none;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:50%;background:#f1ece3;color:#8a7a53;border:1px solid #e0d8c8;
    font-size:11px;font-weight:500;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;transition:background .18s ease,color .18s ease,border-color .18s ease}
  .zmm__field.is-done .zmm__num{background:var(--wine,#7a1f34);color:#fff;border-color:var(--wine,#7a1f34)}
  .zmm__fname{font-size:var(--zf-label-size);letter-spacing:var(--zf-label-track);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--zf-label);line-height:1.4}
  .zmm__fname .u{color:#b3aca0;letter-spacing:.02em}

  @media(max-width:620px){
    .zmm__visual{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .zmm__figure{position:static;max-width:190px;margin:0 auto}
    .zmm__fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  }
</style>

<div class="zmm" data-zmm{% if zmm_nocust %} data-zmm-readyonly{% endif %}{% if zmm_customonly %} data-zmm-customonly{% endif %}>
  <div class="zmm__top">
    <div>
      {%- comment -%}
        No heading where the two buttons are the heading (client, 2026-11-17). "Ready to Wear"
        and "Made to Order" say what the choice is better than "Choose your size" did. It stays
        on the two pages that show no buttons: a finished piece, which has a size rather than a
        choice, and the design brief, which is made to order and says so.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign zmm_head = '' -%}
      {%- if zmm_customonly -%}{%- assign zmm_head = 'Made to order' -%}
      {%- elsif zmm_nocust -%}{%- assign zmm_head = 'Size' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if zmm_head != blank -%}
        <p class="zmm__head">{{ zmm_head }} <span class="req">*</span></p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p class="zmm__sub" data-zmm-sub>{% if zmm_customonly %}Cut to your own measurements, in inches with the centimetre in brackets. Our designer confirms them with you at the fitting.{% elsif zmm_nocust %}This piece is finished in the atelier and comes in a standard size. For a piece cut to your own measurements, start a brief in <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/design-your-look">Design Your Look</a>.{% else %}{% endif %}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="zmm__modes"{% if zmm_nocust or zmm_customonly %} hidden{% endif %}>
    {%- unless zmm_customonly -%}
    <label class="zmm__mode" data-zmm-modelabel>
      <input type="radio" name="properties[Size Type]" value="Ready to Wear" data-zmm-mode="ready" required{% if zmm_nocust %} checked{% endif %}>
      Ready to Wear
    </label>
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- unless zmm_nocust -%}
    <label class="zmm__mode" data-zmm-modelabel>
      <input type="radio" name="properties[Size Type]" value="Made to Order" data-zmm-mode="custom"{% if zmm_customonly %} checked{% endif %}>
      Made to Order
    </label>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ===== READY TO WEAR ===== {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign zmm_len = product.metafields.custom.length.value -%}
  {%- assign zmm_slv = product.metafields.custom.sleeve_length.value -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Two kinds of ready-to-wear piece sit behind this panel. One is already finished in the atelier
    at the length it has, so the size is a statement rather than a choice: that is the piece with a
    length metafield, or one carrying "No Customisation". The other is cut to order in a standard
    size — the Ramadan 2027 jalabiyas — and for those "One Size" said nothing. They ask instead for
    the three figures the cutter needs: the size, the length and the sleeve. The full ten
    measurements are taken at the fitting.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign zmm_fixed = false -%}
  {%- if zmm_len != blank -%}{%- assign zmm_fixed = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if zmm_nocust -%}{%- assign zmm_fixed = true -%}{%- endif -%}

  {%- unless zmm_customonly -%}
  <div class="zmm__panel" data-zmm-panel="ready" hidden>
    {%- if zmm_fixed -%}
    <div class="zmm__ready-grid">
      <div class="zmm__label">Length <span class="req">*</span></div>
      {%- comment -%}
        The piece's own length first, then every inch below it down to 50 (client, 2026-11-16:
        "bring back all 55, 54, 53, 52, 51, 50, all lesser than 56"). Cloth can be taken up and
        cannot be let down, so the ladder only ever runs downwards from what the piece is: a
        57 in piece offers 57 to 50, a 54 in piece offers 54 to 50.

        It is built by counting down rather than with a range, because Liquid ranges only run
        upwards and cannot be reversed. The first turn of the loop is the piece's own length,
        which is why that one carries `selected`.

        This replaces the version that printed a fixed 53 to 61 ladder with everything but one
        rung struck through as "not available", which read as a piece out of stock in eight
        lengths and was asked about as exactly that.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <select name="properties[Length]" data-zmm-in="ready" disabled>
        {%- if zmm_len != blank -%}
          {%- assign zlen_i = zmm_len | plus: 0 -%}
          {%- assign zlen_span = zlen_i | minus: 50 -%}
          {%- if zlen_span < 0 -%}{%- assign zlen_span = 0 -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- for zstep in (0..zlen_span) -%}
            {%- assign zlen_opt = zlen_i | minus: zstep -%}
            {%- assign zmm_lcm = zlen_opt | times: 2.54 | round: 0 -%}
            <option value="{{ zlen_opt }} in ({{ zmm_lcm }} cm)"{% if zstep == 0 %} selected{% endif %}>{{ zlen_opt }} in ({{ zmm_lcm }} cm)</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <option value="One Size" selected>One Size</option>
        {%- endif -%}
      </select>
      <div class="zmm__chart">{% render 'zaria-size-chart' %}</div>
    </div>
    <input type="hidden" name="properties[Size]" value="One Size" data-zmm-in="ready" disabled>
    {%- assign zmm_len_cm = zmm_len | times: 2.54 | round: 0 -%}
    {%- assign zmm_slv_cm = zmm_slv | times: 2.54 | round: 0 -%}
    <p class="zmm__hint">{% if zmm_len != blank %}This piece is finished at <b>{{ zmm_len }} in ({{ zmm_len_cm }} cm)</b> and can be taken up to any shorter length above{% else %}This piece comes in <b>one standard length</b>{% endif %}{% if zmm_slv != blank %}, with a {{ zmm_slv }} in ({{ zmm_slv_cm }} cm) sleeve{% endif %}. Open the <b>Size Chart</b> for full measurements{% unless zmm_nocust %}, or choose <b>Made to Order</b> to have it cut to your own measurements{% endunless %}.{% if zmm_nocust %} For a longer one, we cut to your own measurements in <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/design-your-look">Design Your Look</a>.{% endif %}</p>
    {%- else -%}
    <div class="zmm__fields zmm__fields--ready">
      {%- comment -%}
        No size to pick on this side (client, 2026-11-16: "if it's ready made then there
        shouldn't be size options, only length adjustment options"). Ready to Wear is the house
        standard size, so the only two things left to settle are the length and the sleeve. The
        French ladder is gone with it; a Made to Order piece is cut to the
        customer's own ten measurements. The size still travels with the order, as a word.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="properties[Size]" value="Standard" data-zmm-in="ready" disabled>
      <div class="zmm__field">
        <div class="zmm__fhead"><span class="zmm__fname">Length</span></div>
        <select name="properties[Length]" data-zmm-in="ready" disabled>
          <option value="Standard 61 in (155 cm)" selected>Standard 61 in (155 cm)</option>
          {%- for h in (100..130) -%}
            {%- assign whole = h | divided_by: 2 -%}
            {%- assign rem = h | modulo: 2 -%}
            {%- if rem == 0 -%}{%- capture lab -%}{{ whole }}{%- endcapture -%}{%- else -%}{%- capture lab -%}{{ whole }}.5{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign labcm = h | times: 1.27 | round: 0 -%}
            <option value="{{ lab }} in ({{ labcm }} cm)">{{ lab }} in ({{ labcm }} cm)</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="zmm__field">
        <div class="zmm__fhead"><span class="zmm__fname">Sleeve Length</span></div>
        <select name="properties[Sleeve Length]" data-zmm-in="ready" disabled>
          <option value="Standard for the size chosen" selected>Standard</option>
          {%- for h in (52..68) -%}
            {%- assign whole = h | divided_by: 2 -%}
            {%- assign rem = h | modulo: 2 -%}
            {%- if rem == 0 -%}{%- capture lab -%}{{ whole }}{%- endcapture -%}{%- else -%}{%- capture lab -%}{{ whole }}.5{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign labcm = h | times: 1.27 | round: 0 -%}
            <option value="{{ lab }} in ({{ labcm }} cm)">{{ lab }} in ({{ labcm }} cm)</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="zmm__readyfoot">
      <p class="zmm__hint">Cut to order in our standard size; bust, waist and hip follow the <b>Size Chart</b>. The length and the sleeve are yours to set, and left as they are they come at the standard.</p>
      <div class="zmm__chart">{% render 'zaria-size-chart' %}</div>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- endunless -%}

  {%- comment -%} ===== CUSTOMIZED (visual) ===== {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless zmm_nocust -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Seven measurements, not ten (client, 2026-11-16: "the stricked sizes only remove not all").
    Sleeve Loose, Sleeve Open and Bottom Open were struck off the screenshot: the three a
    customer cannot take on themselves. The sketch lost their three points with them and the
    rest are renumbered 1 to 7, so the circles still answer the fields beside them.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="zmm__panel" data-zmm-panel="custom" hidden>
    <div class="zmm__visual">
      <div class="zmm__figure" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- comment -%}
          The client's own measurement guide, their artwork rather than a redraw of it. Two
          attempts at drawing it by hand came back as "the shape and measurement marking is
          different on our drawing" (2026-11-17), and they were right: the sleeve hang, the
          A-line and where the chest line meets the body are all particular. Their PNG is
          trimmed to the figure and shipped as assets/zaria-measure-guide.png.

          What it costs: the numbers are printed into the picture, so a point no longer lights
          up when its field is focused. The script that did that is guarded on the element and
          simply finds nothing. If that interaction is ever wanted back, the drawing has to
          become an SVG again, with their file as the thing to trace.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="zmm__guidewrap">
          <img src="{{ 'zaria-measure-guide.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Where each measurement is taken on the jalabiya" loading="lazy" width="567" height="912" class="zmm__guide">
          {%- comment -%}
            A live dot sits exactly over each printed one, so a measurement fills in on the
            drawing as it is answered (client, 2026-11-17: "the dot fill dynamically"). The
            numbers are baked into the artwork and cannot change, so these cover them rather
            than replace them. Their positions were measured off the file itself, as a
            percentage of its width and height, so they hold at any size the column takes.
            They carry data-zmm-mark, which is what the script already looks for.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="1" style="left:64.85%;top:15.82%" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="2" style="left:54.11%;top:5.72%" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="3" style="left:18.5%;top:22.86%" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="4" style="left:81.73%;top:19.26%" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="5" style="left:54.55%;top:28.5%" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="6" style="left:53.95%;top:39.16%" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="7" style="left:54.48%;top:53.31%" aria-hidden="true">7</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="8" style="left:4.76%;top:66.34%" aria-hidden="true">8</span>
          <span class="zmm__dot" data-zmm-mark="9" style="left:74.64%;top:3.17%" aria-hidden="true">9</span>
        </div>
        <p class="zmm__figcap">Where we measure</p>
        {%- comment -%}The two things the client's guide asks for before a tape is picked up.{%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="zmm__figsay">Lay a well-fitting jalabiya flat and smooth before measuring.<br>
          Chest, waist and hips are <b>flat widths</b> across the garment, not around the body.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        {%- comment -%}
          No counter. "0 of 8 measurements added" announced what had not been done yet, above a
          form that already shows it: a filled field is marked and its point on the drawing
          lights up (client, 2026-11-17). The script that keeps the count is guarded on the
          element, so it simply finds nothing now and the marks still answer.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="zmm__fields">
          {%- for f in zmm_fields -%}
            {%- assign fp = f | split: ':' -%}
            {%- assign flabel = fp[0] -%}
            {%- assign hmin = fp[1] | plus: 0 -%}
            {%- assign hmax = fp[2] | plus: 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%}An odd number of fields leaves the last one alone on its row; give it the width.{%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign zf_full = '' -%}
            {%- assign zf_odd = zmm_fields.size | modulo: 2 -%}
            {%- if forloop.last and zf_odd == 1 -%}{%- assign zf_full = ' zmm__field--full' -%}{%- endif -%}
            <div class="zmm__field{{ zf_full }}" data-zmm-field="{{ forloop.index }}">
              <div class="zmm__fhead">
                <span class="zmm__num">{{ forloop.index }}</span>
                <span class="zmm__fname">{{ flabel }}</span>
              </div>
              {%- if fp[3] != blank -%}<span class="zmm__fsay">{{ fp[3] }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              <select name="properties[{{ flabel }}]" data-zmm-req data-zmm-in="custom" data-zmm-field-select="{{ forloop.index }}" disabled>
                <option value="">Select</option>
                {%- for h in (hmin..hmax) -%}
                  {%- assign whole = h | divided_by: 2 -%}
                  {%- assign rem = h | modulo: 2 -%}
                  {%- if rem == 0 -%}{%- capture lab -%}{{ whole }}{%- endcapture -%}{%- else -%}{%- capture lab -%}{{ whole }}.5{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign labcm = h | times: 1.27 | round: 0 -%}
                  <option value="{{ lab }} in ({{ labcm }} cm)">{{ lab }} in ({{ labcm }} cm)</option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endunless -%}

  {%- comment -%} ===== SHEILA (abayas) + COMMENT ===== {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if zmm_is_abaya or zmm_show_comment -%}
  <div class="zmm__panel" data-zmm-panel="extra" hidden>
    <div class="zmm__fields" style="margin-top:14px">
      {%- if zmm_is_abaya -%}
      <div class="zmm__field zmm__field--full">
        <div class="zmm__fhead"><span class="zmm__fname">Sheila</span></div>
        <select name="properties[Sheila]" data-zmm-in="extra" disabled>
          <option value="With Sheila">With Sheila</option>
          <option value="Without Sheila">Without Sheila</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if zmm_show_comment -%}
      <div class="zmm__field zmm__field--full">
        <div class="zmm__fhead"><span class="zmm__fname">Comment / special request</span></div>
        <textarea name="properties[Comment]" data-zmm-in="extra" rows="3" placeholder="Anything we should know (preferences, deadline, occasion)…" disabled></textarea>
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Only true of the Made to Order side, so it is shown only there. It sits outside the panel
    above because that panel is not always rendered: the design brief asks for this form with
    show_comment false, and on a piece that is not an abaya there would be nothing left to
    hold the note. The script finds it from the form root, not from the panel.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless zmm_nocust -%}<p class="zmm__hint" data-zmm-customnote hidden>A piece cut to your own measurements cannot be exchanged for fit.</p>{%- endunless -%}
</div>

<script>
  (function(){
    var root = document.currentScript && document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
    if(!root || !root.matches('[data-zmm]')){ root = document.querySelector('[data-zmm]'); }
    if(!root) return;
    var modes = root.querySelectorAll('input[data-zmm-mode]');
    var labels = root.querySelectorAll('[data-zmm-modelabel]');
    var countEl = root.querySelector('[data-zmm-count]');
    function panel(name){ return root.querySelector('[data-zmm-panel="'+name+'"]'); }
    function mark(n){ return root.querySelector('[data-zmm-mark="'+n+'"]'); }

    function refreshProgress(){
      var done = 0;
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-zmm-field-select]').forEach(function(sel){
        var n = sel.getAttribute('data-zmm-field-select');
        var field = root.querySelector('[data-zmm-field="'+n+'"]');
        var m = mark(n);
        var filled = !!sel.value;
        if(filled) done++;
        if(field) field.classList.toggle('is-done', filled);
        if(m) m.classList.toggle('is-done', filled);
      });
      if(countEl) countEl.textContent = done;
    }

    function setActive(which){
      ['ready','custom'].forEach(function(n){ var p=panel(n); if(p) p.hidden = (n!==which); });
      var extra = panel('extra'); if(extra) extra.hidden = false;
      var cnote = root.querySelector('[data-zmm-customnote]'); if(cnote) cnote.hidden = (which !== 'custom');
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-zmm-in]').forEach(function(el){
        var grp = el.getAttribute('data-zmm-in');
        var on = (grp === which) || (grp === 'extra');
        el.disabled = !on;
        if(el.hasAttribute('data-zmm-req')) el.required = on;
      });
      labels.forEach(function(l){ var r=l.querySelector('input'); l.classList.toggle('is-active', !!(r&&r.checked)); });
      if(which==='custom') refreshProgress();
    }
    modes.forEach(function(r){ r.addEventListener('change', function(){ setActive(r.getAttribute('data-zmm-mode')==='ready'?'ready':'custom'); }); });

    // Nothing to choose at either end: open on the only side there is.
    if(root.hasAttribute('data-zmm-readyonly')) setActive('ready');
    if(root.hasAttribute('data-zmm-customonly')) setActive('custom');

    // per-field: update progress + light up the matching diagram point on focus
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-zmm-field-select]').forEach(function(sel){
      var n = sel.getAttribute('data-zmm-field-select');
      sel.addEventListener('change', refreshProgress);
      sel.addEventListener('focus', function(){ var m=mark(n); if(m) m.classList.add('is-active'); });
      sel.addEventListener('blur', function(){ var m=mark(n); if(m) m.classList.remove('is-active'); });
    });

    var form = root.closest('form');
    if(form){
      form.addEventListener('submit', function(e){
        var chosen = root.querySelector('input[data-zmm-mode]:checked');
        if(!chosen){ e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); alert('Please choose Ready to Wear or Made to Order before adding to bag.'); return; }
        var missing = null;
        root.querySelectorAll('[data-zmm-req]').forEach(function(el){
          if(!el.disabled && !el.value && !missing) missing = el;
        });
        if(missing){ e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); missing.focus(); alert('Please complete all required size fields.'); }
      }, true);
    }
  })();
</script>
